  "score_support_basis": "The SCRS rationale concludes the comment deserves a score of 3, which contradicts the gold label of 5. The rationale makes a material error in rubric application by requiring explicit naming of a specific paper section, which is not required for the highest score.",
  "error_sentences": [
    {
      "sentence": "Thus, the grounding is weak; the authors cannot confidently pinpoint the exact part.",
      "error_type": "rubric_misapplication",
      "explanation": "The scoring criteria for score 5 states that the addressed part only needs to be obvious to the authors, it does not require explicit naming of a section, table or figure. The comment clearly addresses the performance comparison between NeuroLM and LaBraM, which is obvious to the paper authors, so grounding is not weak. This claim incorrectly demands explicit section naming, misapplying the rubric."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "Therefore, the comment is weakly grounded but specific, aligning with score 3.",
      "error_type": "score_mapping_error",
      "explanation": "The reasoning incorrectly maps the assessment to score 3, when the comment meets all criteria for the gold score 5: the addressed part is obvious to authors, and the comment clearly specifies what needs to be added/emphasized."
    }
  ],
  "overall_basis": "The SCRS rationale incorrectly assesses grounding and maps to the wrong score, supporting an incorrect score instead of the gold label 5."
}
